+## Shared local library
+
+Use the installed `calmlib.telegram` from PR 14 (revision `5f1eff9a46ab4cdf5f5d53ad1194905e5e12687f`)
+for cache, folders, archive, media and bot registry work. Run scripts with the consuming project's
+venv, or `~/calm/framework/tools/calm-env/.venv/bin/python`; install the shared revision there
+before switching a consumer.
+
+Machine paths and account ids come from `CALMLIB_TELEGRAM_CONFIG`, defaulting to
+`~/calm/config/telegram/telegram.toml`. See `calmlib.telegram.config` for the schema.
+For offline reads, use `store.messages_collection("primary")`, `archive.messages("primary", chat_id)`
+(or `archive.read_lines(path, offset)` for an explicit export), `folders.cached_folders(user_id)`
+and `bots.Registry.load()`. Resolve user ids with `store.account_user_id("primary")`.
+Use `folders.upsert_folder(client, title, ...)` for an already-authorized folder update;
+`start_bots=True` explicitly permits sending `/start`.
+
